Data licence — data-analysed releases
=====================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. It does not
cover the data published in this repository's releases, and no licence is
granted over that data.

The releases here are internal telemetry, published because the pipeline runs
in the open rather than as a dataset offered for reuse:

  * health-log.jsonl - one row per venue per hourly cycle, recording whether
    that venue's retrieval is behaving. Drives the status panel on
    clusterflick.com and the venue health badge.
  * llm-usage-log.jsonl - one row per transform run, recording what the
    pipeline spent on LLM calls. Drives the LLM usage badge.

Concretely:

  * No licence is granted over these releases.
  * There are no schema guarantees. The row shapes change whenever the jobs
    writing them need them to — without notice and without a deprecation
    period.
  * There is no warranty and no guarantee of accuracy, availability or
    continuity. Releases can stop, be deleted or be restructured at any time.

